schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Other Chains and Ecosystems
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: comparison
  summary: >-
    A comparison of five blockchain ecosystems beyond Ethereum — Solana,
    Cosmos, Polkadot, Avalanche, and Near — covering each chain's core
    mechanism, tradeoffs, and relevance to regenerative-finance projects
    (micro-donation/carbon-credit throughput, sovereign community-currency
    chains, shared-security launches, custom subnets, and accessibility/
    climate focus respectively). Closes with a four-factor decision framework
    for choosing where to build (team skills, transaction needs, community
    location, project type).
  audience: individuals evaluating which blockchain ecosystem fits a regenerative project
  known_tensions: []
  related_concepts:
    - chain-selection-tradeoffs
  related_resources:
    - solana
    - cosmos
    - polkadot
    - avalanche
    - near-protocol
